{"event": "the setup of the run in which the person types /rec:hi, whose step runs rec-bin of the plugin's bin/ by its name, then has a background subagent run rec-bin", "claude": "claude -p --input-format stream-json --output-format stream-json --verbose --model haiku --dangerously-skip-permissions --plugin-dir <plugin>", "version": "2.1.328 (Claude Code)", "entry_writes": "each event's one entry runs python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py, which appends the payload it reads on stdin to a file, with the base directories that the transcript then holds", "plugin_files": {".claude-plugin/plugin.json": {"name": "rec", "version": "0.0.1", "description": "Throwaway plugin that logs each hook event's payload"}, "agents/sleeper.md": "---\nname: sleeper\ndescription: Runs the commands its prompt gives, one at a time, in the foreground, and replies with one word.\ntools: Bash\n---\nRun each command your prompt gives, in order, one at a time, in the foreground, and wait for each\nto end. Then reply with the word your prompt gives. Install nothing, and send nothing to any\noutside service.\n", "bin/rec-bin": "#!/bin/sh\n# Prints where the shell found this command, which shows that the plugin's bin/ is on the PATH.\necho \"rec-bin ran from $0\"\n", "hooks/hooks.json": {"hooks": {"SessionStart": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "SessionEnd": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "UserPromptSubmit": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "UserPromptExpansion": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "PreToolUse": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "PostToolUse": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "PostToolUseFailure": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "PermissionRequest": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "PermissionDenied": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "Notification": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "Stop": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "StopFailure": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "SubagentStart": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "SubagentStop": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "PreCompact": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "PostCompact": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "TaskCreated": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "TaskCompleted": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "TeammateIdle": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "InstructionsLoaded": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "ConfigChange": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "CwdChanged": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "Elicitation": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}], "ElicitationResult": [{"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log.py"}]}]}}, "hooks/log.py": "\"\"\"Append the hook payload read on stdin, with the time it came, as one JSON line to $REC_LOG, and\nthe first line of each text of a user message in the transcript at `transcript_path` that opens\n`Base directory for this skill:`, as the transcript holds it when the hook runs.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport time\n\nBASE = \"Base directory for this skill:\"\n\n\ndef texts(text):\n    \"\"\"Each text of the transcript's line, where it's a user message.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        entry = json.loads(text)\n    except ValueError:\n        return []\n    content = entry.get(\"message\", {}).get(\"content\") if entry.get(\"type\") == \"user\" else None\n    return (\n        [part.get(\"text\", \"\") for part in content if isinstance(part, dict)]\n        if isinstance(content, list)\n        else []\n    )\n\n\ndef base_directories(path):\n    if not path or not os.path.exists(path):\n        return []\n    with open(path) as transcript:\n        return [\n            said.split(\"\\n\", 1)[0]\n            for text in transcript\n            for said in texts(text)\n            if said.startswith(BASE)\n        ]\n\n\npayload = json.load(sys.stdin)\nkept = {\n    \"time\": time.time(),\n    \"payload\": payload,\n    \"base_directories\": base_directories(payload.get(\"transcript_path\")),\n}\nwith open(os.environ[\"REC_LOG\"], \"a\") as log:\n    log.write(json.dumps(kept) + \"\\n\")\n", "skills/hi/SKILL.md": "---\nname: hi\ndescription: Runs the plugin's own command rec-bin by its name and replies with one word.\n---\nInstall nothing, and send nothing to any outside service.\n\n1. Run the Bash command `rec-bin`.\n2. Reply with the word hi.\n", "skills/other/SKILL.md": "---\nname: other\ndescription: Runs one echo command.\ndisable-model-invocation: true\n---\nInstall nothing, and send nothing to any outside service.\n\n1. Run the Bash command `echo other-ran`.\n2. Reply with the word other.\n", "skills/start/SKILL.md": "---\nname: start\ndescription: Starts the sleeper subagent in the background and returns at once.\ndisable-model-invocation: true\n---\nInstall nothing, and send nothing to any outside service.\n\n1. Start the subagent rec:sleeper by the Agent tool with run_in_background set to true, the\n   description `Sleep then echo`, and the prompt: `Run the Bash command python3 -c \"import time;\n   time.sleep(30)\" in the foreground. Then run the Bash command echo after-sleep. Then reply with\n   the word slept.`\n2. Don't wait for it. Reply with the word started.\n"}}
